# ADR-NNNN: Decision title

```adr-metadata
{
  "id": "NNNN",
  "title": "Decision title",
  "status": "Proposed",
  "owner": "Decision owner",
  "recorded_date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "decision_date": null,
  "approval_reference": null,
  "supersedes": [],
  "superseded_by": [],
  "replacement_scope": {},
  "retirement": null
}
```

## Scope

Decision question and exactly where it applies; replacement and remaining scope,
if any. Separate decision authority from permission to implement or operate.

## Context

Relevant constraints and source-grounded historical facts; unknowns labeled.

## Alternatives

Credible alternatives and their tradeoffs; avoid inventing historical reasoning.

## Decision

Proposed choice, or actual accepted/rejected disposition with owner evidence.

## Consequences

Benefits, costs and practical limits; status is not deployment evidence.

## Revisit

Conditions that would justify a successor decision.

## Evidence and follow-up

Relevant source links, approval evidence and implementation initiatives;
otherwise the owner and next action. Unverified reports remain attributed.
